  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Energy Small and Medium Enterprises&apos; support in SubSaharan Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The development objective of this trust fund is to support additional  financing and technical assistance activities designed to strengthen  SMEs in providing energy services to poor communities in five to seven  Sub-Saharan Africa.
 
   The Government of Russia has asked the World Bank to manage this  trust fund and to provide technical and fiduciary oversight. The  Africa Energy Unit (AFTEG) will manage the funds under standard World  Bank procedures. AFTEG will oversee the implementation of the trust  fund activities in line with the Africa Energy Strategy with a view to  promoting innovative ways of increasing access to energy services in  the region in partnership with small and medium size enterprises.
 
 AFTEG will closely collaborate with GVEP International in the  implementation of this trust fund. GVEP International will provide  technical assistance to SMEs including development of business plans,  assistance in designing innovative projects, facilitation in securing  financing, and knowledge dissemination. The option to use consulting  services other than GVEP International will also be made available to  beneficiaries.The World Bank and  GVEP International  partnership will  be memorialized in a grant agreement to be signed between the Bank and  GVEP International.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
